Description: Declare the licence the way noble's setuptools understands
 mashumaro 3.17 moved to PEP 639: "license" is now an SPDX expression
 string and the build system asks for setuptools 77. noble carries
 setuptools 68.1.2, which validates pyproject.toml against the older
 schema, where "license" must be a table with either a "file" or a "text"
 key -- a bare string matches both definitions and is rejected outright:
 .
   ValueError: invalid pyproject.toml config: `project.license`.
   configuration error: `project.license` must be valid exactly by one
   definition (2 matches found)
 .
 So the licence goes back into a table and the build-system requirement
 drops its floor. The declared licence is the same Apache-2.0 either way,
 and the wheel's metadata carries it in the older field; nothing in the
 built package differs but the spelling.
 .
 resolute and stonking need none of this -- their own archives build this
 source package -- so the patch is in patches/noble/ and is applied to the
 noble build alone.
Author: Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-05
--- a/pyproject.toml	2026-11-05 09:49:01.872967679 -0500
+++ b/pyproject.toml	2026-11-05 09:49:01.884525898 -0500
@@ -1,11 +1,11 @@
 [build-system]
 build-backend = "setuptools.build_meta"
-requires = ["setuptools>=77.0"]
+requires = ["setuptools"]
 
 [project]
 name = "mashumaro"
 version = "3.17"
-license = "Apache-2.0"
+license = { text = "Apache-2.0" }
 description = "Fast and well tested serialization library"
 readme = "README.md"
 authors = [{ name = "Alexander Tikhonov", email = "random.gauss@gmail.com" }]
